[33.472554, "i", "cat > /app/black/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\nBlack Library - Key Functions for Testing\n\nBlack is an uncompromising Python code formatter.\n\nKey Functions and Modules to Test:\n1. black.format_str() - Main function to format Python code strings\n2. black.format_file_in_place() - Format a file in place\n3. black.reformat_many() - Format multiple files\n4. black.lib2to3_parse() - Parse Python code using lib2to3\n5. black.get_features_used() - Detect Python features in code\n6. linegen.LineGenerator - Generate formatted lines from AST\n7. strings.normalize_string() - Normalize string literals\n8. strings.fix_docstring() - Fix docstring formatting\n9. trans.transform_line() - Transform a line of code\n10. comments.normalize_invisible_parens() - Handle invisible parentheses\n11. brackets.get_implied_line_range() - Handle bracket logic\n12. parsing.parse_ast() - Parse Python AST\n13. Mode class - Configuration for formatting behavior\n\nFuzzing Focus Areas:\n- Malformed Python code handling\n- Edge cases in string normalization\n- "]
[33.472706, "o", "cat > /app/black/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\r\n"]
[33.472757, "i", "Comment handling in various positions\n- Large/deeply nested code structures\n- Unicode and special character handling\n- Various Python syntax edge cases\nEOF\n"]
