[89.208401, "i", "cat > /app/ujson/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\nUjson Library - Key Functions for Testing\n\nUjson is an ultra-fast JSON encoder and decoder written in C with Python bindings.\n\nKey Functions to Test:\n1. ujson.loads() - Parse JSON string to Python objects\n2. ujson.dumps() - Encode Python objects to JSON string\n3. ujson.load() - Load JSON from file\n4. ujson.dump() - Dump Python objects to file as JSON\n5. JSONtoObj.c - JSON parsing implementation\n6. objToJSON.c - JSON encoding implementation\n\nKey Parameters and Options:\n- encode_html_chars - Escape HTML characters in output\n- escape_forward_slashes - Escape forward slashes\n- ensure_ascii - Escape non-ASCII characters\n- sort_keys - Sort object keys in output\n- indent - Pretty-print with indentation\n- default - Custom encoder for non-serializable objects\n- object_hook - Custom decoder hook for objects\n- parse_float - Custom float parser\n- parse_int - Custom int parser\n\nFuzzing Focus Areas:\n- Malformed JSON strings (invalid syntax, incomplete structures)\n- Deeply nes"]
[89.208474, "i", "ted JSON structures (stack overflow testing)\n- Large JSON payloads (memory exhaustion)\n- Unicode and escape sequence handling\n- Numeric edge cases (very large numbers, NaN, Infinity)\n- Circular reference detection\n- Custom encoder/decoder hook edge cases\n- Empty and null value handling\n- Array and object boundary conditions\nEOF\n"]
[89.208622, "o", "cat > /app/ujson/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\r\n> "]
